      "created_at": "2018-07-27T12:21:43Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-07-27T12:21:43Z",
      "body": "So I've looked into this from a UI perspective. I looked at:\r\n- An input field\r\n- Radio buttons\r\n- Drop down\r\n\r\nhttps://xd.adobe.com/view/f455f026-ce60-4549-4a8d-7118c34b9bba-8264/?fullscreen\r\n\r\nThere's 5 pages in the prototype to click through\r\n\r\nInput field is a no, it's too complicated to figure out the increments system and I suspect would have a lot of human error.\r\n\r\nRadio buttons is usable, accessible and works but a bit long.\r\n\r\nDrop down is the same as radio but saves on vertical screen space. So my vote is on that one. Comments, amends and extra info I may not have considered always very welcome though! (also sorry for the delay on this one)\r\n\r\nThe main thing I'd like to make sure happens is that the copy for the 'most anonymised' and 'least anonymised' option is included. That way the users can make an informed decision using this and also if they have an understanding of km/m in relation to the data they're capturing it'll help.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
